{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Los Angeles RSO relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord who terminates a tenancy under the Rent Stabilization Ordinance must pay relocation assistance by tenant income and tenancy length — $11,000 or $14,400 to eligible tenants, $23,150 or $27,400 to qualified tenants — within 15 days of serving the eviction notice.","key_value":"Eligible tenant $11,000 (<3 yrs) / $14,400 (3+ yrs or low income); qualified tenant $23,150 / $27,400; July 1, 2026–June 30, 2027","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced by a no-fault termination of an RSO-covered rental unit in the City of Los Angeles; relocation is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO-covered rental units in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":"Relocation offset: a landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against relocation assistance, unless a government order to vacate or comply concerns an unpermitted dwelling. (LAMC 151.09.G,5.)","penalty":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an eviction action and may file a complaint with LAHD.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §151.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"CHART A: RSO or JCO Amounts
Effective July 1, 2026 through June 30, 2027 (Increases July 1st)
Household Type Less than 3 Years
3 or More Years or Low
Income
Eligible Tenant $11,000 $14,400
Qualified Tenant $23,150 $27,400","interaction":"Relocation amounts above the RSO or JCO amount under Option 3 are regulated by state law.","confidence":0.78,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord who terminates a tenancy under the Just Cause Ordinance must pay the RSO/JCO relocation amounts, and for a single-family dwelling owned by a natural person, one month's rent as payment or credit.","key_value":"One month's rent for a natural-person-owned single-family dwelling; otherwise Chart A RSO/JCO amounts","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced under the Just Cause Ordinance, including single-family dwellings subject to the JCO owned by a natural person who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"JCO-covered rental units; single-family natural-person owners"},"exemptions":"Relocation offset applies (LAMC 165.06.J); LAMC 151.30(E) does not apply to single-family dwellings owned by natural persons.","penalty":"A tenant may raise failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an eviction action and may file a complaint with LAHD.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §165.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"When the residential real property is a single-family dwelling subject to the JCO and the owner is a natural person, including natural persons who hold properties in a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that natural person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles: one month’s rent that was in effect when the landlord served the written notice to terminate the tenancy, as either a monetary payment or credit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.78,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance new-development relocation payments","requirement":"Only lower-income households displaced by demolition where the owner will replace the units with new construction must receive relocation payments matching the benefits public entities must pay under Government Code Chapter 16.","key_value":"Extremely Low $115,480; Very Low $96,750; Low $87,450 (7/1/2026–6/30/2027)","coverage_conditions":"Only Low, Very Low and Extremely Low income households displaced by new development; above-low-income tenants receive the RSO or JCO amounts.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Lower-income households displaced by demolition and new construction"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO)","quoted_span":"ONLY lower income households being displaced for the purpose of demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction must receive relocation payment consistent to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities pursuant to Chapter 16","interaction":"Required jointly by the City's RPO and the State's Housing Crisis Act (HCA).","confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
